{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "03894b01-fff4-89e5-ba4c-341c73fab647",
  "created_at": "2026-01-07T10:46:01-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Finance",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Colin Doyle",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Luis Barros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:43:45-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Finance department, this is Luis. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:43:50-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning, Luis! Wonderful, I got a person! Colin Doyle here. I'm on the speakerphone, so tell me if I'm too far away from it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:44:00-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're coming through fine, Mr. Doyle. What's going on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:44:04-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, I've got my property tax bill here and it's wrong! It says my house is, um, two thousand four hundred square feet. Great big number. It's not that big! It's nowhere near that. I've lived here a long time, I think I'd know!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:44:20-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Square footage is the assessor's side, not finance. We just send the bill based on what they have on file."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:44:28-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wonderful, so it's a runaround. Great. Well, what are the assessor's office hours then?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:44:34-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "They're open weekdays, generally eight thirty to four thirty, same as City Hall. I'd call ahead, though, so somebody's at the desk. I can transfer you if you want."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:44:45-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, no, I'll call them myself after this. Let me write that down. Eight thirty to four thirty. Great! Now, the installment is due and I don't want to pay extra on a bill that's wrong. If I drop a payment in the box tonight, does that count as on time?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:45:03-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a drop box at City Hall, and it's emptied each business day. If it's in the box by the due date, you're fine. Just make sure the check has your account number on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:45:16-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wonderful! And I can still fight the square footage after I pay?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:45:21-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, paying doesn't stop you from asking the assessor to look at it. That's their call, though."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:45:28-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great! Hold on a second. [pause] Sorry, my smart thermostat is arguing with me. I set it to sixty-eight and it keeps saying it knows better. Seventy! It wants seventy!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:45:39-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sounds like it's got opinions. I can't help with that one, Mr. Doyle. Pretty sure that's not a city department."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:45:47-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ha! No, I suppose not! Anyway, wonderful, thank you. Eight thirty to four thirty, drop box tonight, and call the assessor."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:45:55-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it. Good luck with the house and the thermostat."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T10:45:59-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great, thanks, Luis! Goodbye!"
    }
  ],
